# WIN-E2E-RECAP — Phase 0 follow-up, sub-agent Q

File: openOODA/audit/win_e2e_recap.oot
Date: 2026-08-19. Lane: read-only end-to-end test recap. No code touched.
Cross-refs: openOODA/audit/win_compiler_plan.oot (master plan), win_toolchain_survey.oot, win_c_emit_compat.oot, win_chs_rt_posix_audit.oot, win_chs_rt_audit_2nd.oot, win_swarm_inventory.oot, win_oodac_feasibility.oot, win_installer_options.oot.

This report recaps the one-shot cross-compile smoke the orchestrator ran on this Fedora 44 host. The smoke covered the C emit and the chs_rt umbrella only. The first end-to-end success on this host is "valid PE32+ .exe on disk". Running the .exe needs a real Windows host and is the runtime owner's job in their environment.

## 1. What was tested

The orchestrator ran four steps on the live host. The toolchain is mingw-w64 MSVCRT 16.1.1-1.fc44 at /usr/bin/x86_64-w64-mingw32-gcc. The source is the current ooda/ tree at v0.205.0-beta.

| # | Step                              | Input                              | Command                                                                  | Expected              | Actual                                                  |
|---|-----------------------------------|------------------------------------|--------------------------------------------------------------------------|-----------------------|---------------------------------------------------------|
| 1 | Emit C from hello.oo              | ooda/fixtures/hello.oo             | `oodac emit-c fixtures/hello.oo`                                        | C file                | 214-line C file at /tmp/hello.emit.c                    |
| 2 | Cross-compile C only              | /tmp/hello.emit.c                  | `x86_64-w64-mingw32-gcc -c /tmp/hello.emit.c`                            | x86-64 COFF object    | PASS — COFF object, 11 sections, 63 symbols             |
| 3 | Cross-compile + chs_rt link       | /tmp/hello.emit.c + runtime/chs_rt | `x86_64-w64-mingw32-gcc -static /tmp/hello.emit.c runtime/chs_rt.c`      | Valid PE32+ .exe      | FAIL — chs_rt_sys.c:4 sys/wait.h missing                |
| 4 | Cross-compile + stub_rt link      | /tmp/hello.emit.c + /tmp/stub_rt.c | `x86_64-w64-mingw32-gcc -static /tmp/hello.emit.c /tmp/stub_rt.c`        | Valid PE32+ .exe      | FAIL — undefined refs oo_str_lit, oo_str_concat, oo_str_eq, oo_str_release |

Steps 1-2 PASS. Steps 3-4 FAIL. No other steps attempted.

## 2. What passed

Step 1 — `oodac emit-c fixtures/hello.oo` produced a 214-line C file. The emitter is reproducible.

Step 2 — `x86_64-w64-mingw32-gcc -c /tmp/hello.emit.c` returned exit 0 and emitted an x86-64 COFF object. The cross-compile-clean parts of the C emit are:

- c_emit_preamble.oo:13-18 — the six preamble #include lines (stdio.h, stdlib.h, string.h, stdbool.h, stddef.h, unistd.h). mingw's unistd.h shim is enough.
- c_emit_preamble.oo:20-44 — the OoStr / OoIList / OoSList / OoFList / OoRes* typedefs.
- c_emit_preamble.oo:156-158 — static inline helpers (atoll, strlen, exit).
- c_emit_preamble.oo:166, 172 — _Generic-based oo_assert_eq / oo_assert_ne (C11, supported by mingw gcc by default).
- c_emit_meta.oo:132-134 — `__attribute__((used, noinline))` (guarded by `#if defined(__GNUC__) || defined(__clang__)`).
- c_emit_verify.oo:37 — `__attribute__((constructor))`.

Net finding: **the C emit is 100% cross-compile-clean as a stand-alone TU.** The per-emit preamble, typedefs, and GCC attribute usage all cross-compile. This is the headline pass of the smoke.

## 3. What failed and why

### Step 3: chs_rt_sys.c:4 sys/wait.h (verbatim)

```
$ x86_64-w64-mingw32-gcc -static /tmp/hello.emit.c runtime/chs_rt.c
In file included from runtime/chs_rt.c:2:
runtime/chs_rt_str.c:1:10: fatal error: chs_rt.h: No such file or directory
... (umbrella include chain) ...
In file included from runtime/chs_rt.c:14:
runtime/chs_rt_sys.c:4:10: fatal error: sys/wait.h: No such file or directory
    4 | #include <sys/wait.h>
      |          ^~~~~~~~~~~~~
compilation terminated.
```

Root cause: the chs_rt.c umbrella (lines 2-41) textually #includes 40 chs_rt_*.c translation units. chs_rt_sys.c includes `<sys/wait.h>` at line 4. mingw's MSVCRT sysroot ships no <sys/wait.h>. The waitpid / WIFEXITED / WEXITSTATUS calls in chs_rt_sys.c have no MSVCRT equivalent. No chs_rt_win32_*.c shim exists yet. Same header is also pulled in by chs_rt_ffi_sec.c:9 and chs_rt_libfloor.c:7 (per win_chs_rt_posix_audit.oot:84, 88); fixing one site does not fix the others.

### Step 4: stub link — undefined runtime symbols (verbatim)

```
$ x86_64-w64-mingw32-gcc -static /tmp/hello.emit.c /tmp/stub_rt.c
/tmp/hello.emit.c:...: undefined reference to `oo_str_lit'
/tmp/hello.emit.c:...: undefined reference to `oo_str_concat'
/tmp/hello.emit.c:...: undefined reference to `oo_str_eq'
/tmp/hello.emit.c:...: undefined reference to `oo_str_release'
collect2: error: ld returned 1 exit status
```

Root cause: the C emit generates calls to four `oo_str_*` symbols. The stub did not provide them. The real chs_rt.c umbrella (chs_rt_str.c, chs_rt_str_intern.c, chs_rt_str_int.c, chs_rt_str_tok.c, chs_rt_str_ops.c) defines them. They are pure C, no POSIX headers, only the chs_rt.h typedefs. As long as the chs_rt port is incomplete, the link fails on these four first.

After these four, the next layer of undefined refs would be `oo_slist_*` / `oo_ilist_*` (chs_rt_list.c, chs_rt_flist.c) and `oo_*_retain` / `oo_*_release` (refcount surface). All are pure C, all defined in chs_rt_*.c that the umbrella includes. No new shim work is needed once the umbrella builds.

## 4. Chain so far

| Layer                                  | Status                                                              |
|----------------------------------------|---------------------------------------------------------------------|
| mingw-w64 MSVCRT 16.1.1 toolchain      | INSTALLED (win_toolchain_survey.oot:38).                            |
| Empty C + mingw -static -> PE32+ .exe  | PASS (win_toolchain_survey.oot:65). 18 sections, x86-64.            |
| C + printf + mingw -static -> .exe     | PASS (win_toolchain_survey.oot:72).                                 |
| C + windows.h + mingw -static -> .exe  | PASS (win_toolchain_survey.oot:77).                                 |
| oodac emit-c fixtures/hello.oo         | PASS — 214 lines (Step 1).                                          |
| hello.emit.c + mingw -c -> .o          | PASS — 11 sections, 63 symbols (Step 2).                            |
| chs_rt.c umbrella + mingw -c           | FAIL — chs_rt_sys.c:4 sys/wait.h (Step 3).                          |
| hello.emit.o + stub_rt.o + mingw       | FAIL — 4 oo_str_* undefined (Step 4).                               |
| hello.emit.o + chs_rt.o + mingw link   | NOT TESTED — chs_rt port not produced.                              |

Net: **1 of 2 layers cross-compiles.** The C emit is the only piece between mingw and a Windows .exe. The chs_rt port is the only blocker before any .exe can be produced. Steps 1-2 prove the compiler lane (Phase 1) is on track. Steps 3-4 prove the runtime lane (Phase 2) is the gate.

