## 6. Next concrete test command

Single next test, runnable on this Linux host, after the runtime owner produces a chs_rt_win32_*.c shim that covers at least the headers in chs_rt_sys.c, chs_rt_libfloor.c, and chs_rt_ffi_sec.c:

```
x86_64-w64-mingw32-gcc -c ooda/runtime/chs_rt.c \
  -I/usr/x86_64-w64-mingw32/sys-root/mingw/include \
  -o /tmp/chs_rt.o 2>&1
file /tmp/chs_rt.o
```

Expected to FAIL with the next POSIX-only header in the umbrella include order. Without any shim, it fails immediately at chs_rt_sys.c:4. The shim must cover these headers (each is a different chs_rt_*.c file in the umbrella; full list per win_chs_rt_posix_audit.oot §2 and win_chs_rt_audit_2nd.oot §2):

1. <sys/wait.h> (chs_rt_sys.c:4, chs_rt_ffi_sec.c:9, chs_rt_libfloor.c:7) — today's gate.
2. <sys/types.h> (chs_rt_sys.c:3, chs_rt_caps.c:6, chs_rt_dns.c:5, chs_rt_fetch.c:5, chs_rt_netfloor.c:4, chs_rt_tls.c:4) — POSIX; shim with intptr_t / size_t.
3. <sys/prctl.h> + <sys/syscall.h> (chs_rt_landlock.c:6-7) — Landlock redesign (Job Object + restricted token + NTFS DACL).
4. <sys/resource.h> (chs_rt_rlimit.c:5) — setrlimit redesign.
5. <netdb.h>, <sys/socket.h>, <arpa/inet.h>, <netinet/in.h> (chs_rt_dns.c, chs_rt_netfloor.c, chs_rt_tls.c, chs_rt_fetch.c) — Winsock.
6. <dlfcn.h> (chs_rt_ffi.c:5, chs_rt_ffi_sec.c:8) — LoadLibraryExA.
7. <dirent.h>, <fcntl.h> (chs_rt_fs.c, chs_rt_ffi_sec.c) — FindFirstFile.
8. <sys/random.h> (chs_rt_alloc.c, chs_rt_caps.c, chs_rt_libfloor.c, chs_rt_meta.c, chs_rt_time_rand.c, chs_rt_ffi_sec.c) — BCryptGenRandom.
9. <pthread.h> (10+ files) — link -lpthread (winpthread).
10. <signal.h> + kill (chs_rt_libfloor.c:57, :121) — TerminateProcess.
11. <unistd.h> — shim (already present in mingw).

After #1-#11 land, the chs_rt.c umbrella compiles to /tmp/chs_rt.o. The next test is then the link:

```
x86_64-w64-mingw32-gcc -static /tmp/hello.emit.o /tmp/chs_rt.o \
  -o /tmp/hello.exe \
  -lws2_32 -lbcrypt -ladvapi32 -lkernel32 -lpthread -ldl
file /tmp/hello.exe
```

A passing link produces a real PE32+ .exe. This is the first full-success test of the chain on this Linux host. Running the .exe needs a Windows host; that is the runtime owner's job in their environment.

## 7. What was not tested

- A real Windows host. The .exe was never run; this Linux box cannot run a PE32+ image. The success criterion for the smoke is "valid PE32+ .exe on disk", not "ran and printed OK".
- The chs_rt port. Only the chs_rt umbrella was attempted; the chs_rt_win32_*.c shim is not on disk. Step 3 fails at the first POSIX header; nothing past Step 3 was attempted.
- The cap-require symbol check. ooda/oodac/main.oo:178 calls `nm` to verify cap-require symbols; `nm` is a Linux binutils tool. On Windows the equivalent is `dumpbin /SYMBOLS` or `llvm-readobj --coff-symbols`. Not tested.
- The deterministic-byte lock. Phase 1 acceptance (`scripts/win_cross_hello_smoke.oo`) requires byte-identical output across two runs. The first .exe was not produced, so this lock was not exercised.
- The C++ path. mingw64-gcc-c++ is installed; the C emit is plain C; not exercised.
- The linker link order with -lws2_32 -lbcrypt -ladvapi32 -lkernel32 -lpthread -ldl. Not reached. This is the link step after the shim.
- The post-shim link error chain (pthread, dl, winsock). Not observed.
- chs_rt_vision.c mkdir sites (chs_rt_vision.c:209, 210, 228, 229 per win_chs_rt_audit_2nd.oot:71) and chs_rt_wasm.c:161 fopen /proc/self/cmdline (per win_chs_rt_audit_2nd.oot:70). Both are inside the umbrella; the umbrella fails at chs_rt_sys.c:4 before reaching either; neither was reached.
- The C emit's own host header deps past unistd.h. unistd.h was the only Linux-flavored include in the preamble; mingw's shim covered it. No other host headers were exercised.
- Whether oodac emit-c is target-aware. The current emit is target-agnostic. Phase 1 emit_windows.oo is a future file.
- install_win.oo, openooda.nsi, oodac.exe on Windows. Not produced.
- The chs_rt_list_set.c straggler (per win_chs_rt_audit_2nd.oot §6). Not exercised; outside the umbrella.
- chs_rt.c lines 43-97 (the str_split / str_trim bodies defined in the umbrella itself). Not reached.
- ooda/bootstrap/seed/oodac (the seed binary). Not exercised; the everyday path is a working tree rebuild, and the cross-compile does not use the seed.
- The 4 of 41 chs_rt_*.c files not in the umbrella (chs_rt_list_set.c only; chs_rt_str.c is in the umbrella at chs_rt.c:2 per win_chs_rt_audit_2nd.oot §6). Only the umbrella was attempted.
- pthread / dl / winsock / bcrypt link flags. The orchestrator did not reach the link step; the link flags are predicted from win_c_emit_compat.oot:134, not measured.
- UCRT vs MSVCRT. The host has MSVCRT only (win_toolchain_survey.oot:44). UCRT is not installed. The test cannot compare.

